": -0.00011122845171485096, "top": [["DC", -0.00011122845171485096], ["D", -9.658220291137695]]}, {"t": "MAKE", "lp": -0.00011957406968576834, "top": [["MAKE", -0.00011957406968576834], [" MAKE", -10.235041618347168]]}, {"t": "_INSTALL", "lp": -0.000829563825391233, "top": [["_INSTALL", -0.000829563825391233], [" INSTALL", -8.029242515563965]]}, {"t": "_LIB", "lp": -0.00018294338951818645, "top": [["_LIB", -0.00018294338951818645], [" Lib", -10.327688217163086]]}, {"t": "DIR", "lp": -8.535749657312408e-05, "top": [["DIR", -8.535749657312408e-05], [" DIR", -11.59123706817627]]}, {"t": "=", "lp": -0.0002450647298246622, "top": [["=", -0.0002450647298246622], ["`", -11.69643783569336]]}, {"t": "lib", "lp": -0.0008960803388617933, "top": [["lib", -0.0008960803388617933], [" lib", -9.140514373779297]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.00024244147061835974, "top": [["`", -0.00024244147061835974], [" `", -9.807226181030273]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, not the default GCC.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into broken output.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp`** \u2014 Source directory (where the git repo was checked out)\n- **`-B \"${srcdir}/build`** \u2014 Build directory (where compilation artifacts go)\n- **`-G Ninja`** \u2014 Use the **Ninja** build system generator (fast, efficient alternative to Make)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nCompile in **Release** mode: optimizations enabled (`-O3`), no debug symbols. This is the performance-focused build.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`** \u2014 Where `make install` will place files (standard system location)\n- **`-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib`"}